- `ui-smoke`: 
- `ui-tests`: `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LibraryWindowTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.InverseConstructorTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.LightSourceEditorTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SolverHandoffWindowTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WindowLauncherTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.OutOfBandBadgeTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.FsxAcceptanceTests`

**How to implement.** The UI suite's Library-window and scene facts read the shipped catalogue instead of the code seeds (001 §B 'tests load the same files'; the S1.7 brief: re-point every test that reads a seed value to the BuiltinCatalogue fixture, numbers unchanged). Files, all in `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/`: `LibraryWindowTests.fs`, `InverseConstructorTests.fs`, `LightSourceEditorTests.fs`, `SolverHandoffWindowTests.fs`, `ScrollExtentTests.fs`, `WindowLauncherTests.fs`, `OutOfBandBadgeTests.fs`, `WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests.fs`, `FsxAcceptanceTests.fs`. Re-point rules (S1.7; the same in every re-point step). `builtInEntries` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.materials ()`; `standardCategories` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.categories ()`; `MaterialLibrary.standard` (written `standard` under `open MaterialLibrary`) becomes `{ entries = BuiltinCatalogue.materials () }`; `SeedSamples.allSeedSamples` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.samples ()`; `SeedSamples.<name>` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.sample SampleIds.<name>Id` and `SeedSamples.<name>.id` becomes `SampleIds.<name>Id` (step 15's names); `SeedSources.allSeedSources` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.sources ()`; `SeedSources.reference600` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.source PresetIds.source600`; the `SeedSources.tunables` list becomes `[ PresetIds.xenonMonochromator; PresetIds.tiSapphireTunable; PresetIds.supercontinuum; PresetIds.euvBeamline ] |> List.map BuiltinCatalogue.source`, and one tunable source becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.source PresetIds.xenonMonochromator`; `seedEntries` becomes `(BuiltinCatalogue.samples () |> List.map SampleItem) @ BuiltinCatalogue.presets ()`; `Library.createInMemory ()` (written `createInMemory ()` under `open Library`) becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.library ()`; and the self-seeding stores become the fixture's doubles with the same arguments (step 45): `MaterialProxy.createInMemory r v` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.materialStore r v`, `SampleProxy.createInMemory v` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.sampleStore v` and `CategoryProxy.createInMemory r` becomes `BuiltinCatalogue.categoryStore r`. A fact that took a seed by its list position (`List.head`, `List.item`) takes the same entry by its well-known id (`MaterialIds`, `CategoryIds`, `SampleIds`, `PresetIds`), so it still tests the entry it tested; a fact that compared ordered lists built from the seed lists builds both sides from the fixture, and compares order-independently only where the product's order is not the fixture's row order (the S1.3 step 20 precedent). Every fact keeps its name and its assertions, every count and every number stays. A comment or doc, an `open`'s trailing comment included, that names a seed or a self-seeding store names the fixture member instead, in no more words, and an `open` nothing needs any more goes. No product file, fixture member or fact is added. Per file: `LibraryWindowTests`' `seededCorpus` counts `BuiltinCatalogue.samples ()` plus `BuiltinCatalogue.presets ()`, its kind counts read `List.length (BuiltinCatalogue.sources ())`, and its Library is `BuiltinCatalogue.library ()`; the scenes of `InverseConstructorTests`, `SolverHandoffWindowTests`, `ScrollExtentTests`, `WindowLauncherTests` and `OutOfBandBadgeTests` compose over the doubles; `LightSourceEditorTests` and `WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests` build their `libraryContext` over them; `FsxAcceptanceTests` composes its scene's stores through `materialStore`, `sampleStore`, `categoryStore` and `library ()`, and saves its script materials into them as before, so every script comparison keeps its numbers.

**Acceptance.** After the re-point, `git grep -n -E "SeedSamples|SeedSources|seedEntries|seedTrees|builtInEntries|standardCategories|seedExperiments|(MaterialProxy|SampleProxy|CategoryProxy).createInMemory |Library.createInMemory " -- Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LibraryWindowTests.fs Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/InverseConstructorTests.fs Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/LightSourceEditorTests.fs Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/SolverHandoffWindowTests.fs Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/ScrollExtentTests.fs Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WindowLauncherTests.fs Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/OutOfBandBadgeTests.fs Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/WorkbenchInfoAndCaptureTests.fs Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/FsxAcceptanceTests.fs MUST find nothing; ui-smoke MUST pass with its count unchanged; ui-tests MUST pass over the touched classes with their counts unchanged, FsxAcceptanceTests' script comparisons included; and build, elevation and the seven s07 invariants MUST pass.
